-- ----- fragment: minion_isaiah_62.sql (Isaiah 62) -----
-- Chapter: Isaiah 62 — ZION'S NEW NAME / the married land, the restoration crown. The divorced
-- wife of the prophets (Hosea's Lo-Ammi) is renamed and remarried: *thou shalt be called by a new
-- name, which the mouth of Yahuah (LORD) shall name* (62:2); *Thou shalt no more be termed
-- Forsaken... but thou shalt be called Hephzi-bah, and thy land Beulah: for Yahuah (LORD)
-- delighteth in thee, and thy land shall be married* (62:4); *as the bridegroom rejoiceth over the
-- bride, so shall thy Elohim (God) rejoice over thee* (62:5). This is NOT replacement — it is the
-- SAME scattered, divorced two-house wife restored: Forsaken/Desolate become Delighted-in/Married,
-- Lo-Ammi becomes Ammi. The new name is given to the overcomer (Rev 2:17 / 3:12); the bridegroom
-- is the Formed Son and the restored Yashar'el the bride (Rev 19:7 / 21:2); the coming One brings
-- his reward (62:11 → Rev 22:12); the holy people / redeemed are the peculiar people (62:12 →
-- 1 Peter 2:9-10).
-- Tag: isa62   Temp view: _s303_isa62_lookup
-- Sort band: base 27525, step 3 -> threads at 27525, 27528, 27531, 27534, 27537 (5 threads)
-- Source of EVERY row: 'canon','isaiah',62,v
--
-- Isaiah 62 coverage:
--   v.1  (For Zion's sake will I not hold my peace... until the righteousness thereof go forth)
--        NT:     none warranted distinct (the watchman/intercession reaches its head at v.6-7,
--                woven in the THREAD 2 + THREAD 4 prose; v.1's "I will not rest" is Yahuah's own
--                resolve, the same the watchmen take up)
--        Extras: none warranted
--        Tanakh: woven into prose (the righteousness-as-brightness/salvation-as-lamp)
--   ★★ v.2  (thou shalt be called by a new name, which the mouth of Yahuah (LORD) shall name)
--        NT:     ★★ Revelation 2:17 (a white stone, and in the stone a new name written, which no
--                man knoweth saving he that receiveth it), ★★ Revelation 3:12 (I will write upon
--                him my new name) — THREAD 1 (the new name given to the overcomer)
--        Extras: none warranted (named in prose)
--        Tanakh: ★ Isaiah 62:4 (thou shalt be called Hephzi-bah) — the new name itself; bound in THREAD 2
--   v.3  (a crown of glory in the hand of Yahuah (LORD), and a royal diadem)
--        NT:     none warranted distinct (the crown imagery woven into THREAD 1/THREAD 3 prose)
--        Extras: none warranted
--        Tanakh: held in prose
--   ★★ v.4  (Thou shalt no more be termed Forsaken... Hephzi-bah, and thy land Beulah... thy land
--           shall be married)
--        NT:     none warranted distinct (the Lo-Ammi reversal is Hosea's; the NT marriage is
--                THREAD 3)
--        Extras: none warranted
--        Tanakh: ★★ Hosea 1:10 (in the place where it was said... Ye are not my people, there it
--                shall be said... Ye are the sons of the living Elohim (God)), ★★ Hosea 2:23 (I
--                will say to them which were not my people, Thou art my people), ★ Hosea 2:19 (I
--                will betroth thee unto me for ever) — THREAD 2 (the two-house reversal)
--   ★ v.5  (as the bridegroom rejoiceth over the bride, so shall thy Elohim (God) rejoice over thee)
--        NT:     ★ Revelation 19:7 (the marriage of the Lamb is come, and his wife hath made
--                herself ready), ★ Revelation 21:2 (the holy city, new Jerusalem... prepared as a
--                bride adorned for her husband) — THREAD 3 (the bridegroom and the bride)
--        Extras: none warranted
--        Tanakh: Hosea betrothal woven (cross-linked to THREAD 2)
--   ★ v.6-7 (I have set watchmen upon thy walls... give him no rest, till he establish... Jerusalem
--           a praise in the earth)
--        NT:     none warranted distinct (the ceaseless intercession woven into THREAD 4 prose;
--                no single NT verse forced)
--        Extras: none warranted
--        Tanakh: THREAD 4 anchors on the watchmen (canon-internal, the restoration-crown frame)
--   v.8-9 (Yahuah (LORD) hath sworn... I will no more give thy corn to be meat for thine enemies)
--        NT:     none warranted
--        Extras: none warranted
--        Tanakh: woven into THREAD 4 prose (the reversal of the Deuteronomy 28 curse)
--   v.10 (Go through, go through the gates; prepare ye the way of the people... lift up a standard)
--        NT:     none warranted distinct (prepare-the-way woven in prose; the ensign/standard is
--                the gathering signal, held in THREAD 4)
--        Extras: none warranted
--        Tanakh: THREAD 4 (the highway / the standard for the people)
--   ★★ v.11 (Behold, thy salvation cometh; behold, his reward is with him, and his work before him)
--        NT:     ★★ Revelation 22:12 (behold, I come quickly; and my reward is with me, to give
--                every man according as his work shall be) — THREAD 5 (the coming One brings his reward)
--        Extras: none warranted
--        Tanakh: woven (daughter of Zion / the proclamation to the end of the world)
--   ★ v.12 (they shall call them, The holy people, The redeemed of Yahuah (LORD)... A city not forsaken)
--        NT:     ★ 1 Peter 2:9 (a chosen generation, a royal priesthood, an holy nation, a peculiar
